WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.832
Here is our learning path for this module.

00:00:02.832 --> 00:00:06.872
We are going to work through five main ideas.

00:00:06.872 --> 00:00:10.527
The first topic is list comprehensions.

00:00:10.527 --> 00:00:15.797
A list comprehension gives us a compact way to create a new list from an existing collection of

00:00:15.797 --> 00:00:19.262
values. Next, we will look at lambda functions.

00:00:19.262 --> 00:00:24.812
A lambda is basically a very small function that we can define in one expression.

00:00:24.812 --> 00:00:30.922
You will often see lambda functions used with operations such as sorting.

00:00:30.922 --> 00:00:33.057
After that, we will study generators.

00:00:33.057 --> 00:00:39.912
Generators are useful when we want Python to produce values one at a time instead of creating everything

00:00:39.912 --> 00:00:43.272
in memory at once. Then we will discuss debugging.

00:00:43.272 --> 00:00:47.392
Even experienced programmers spend a lot of time debugging.

00:00:47.392 --> 00:00:53.792
So we will look at simple techniques for understanding what is happening inside our code.

00:00:53.792 --> 00:00:58.302
Finally, we will discuss efficiency and built-in Python functions.

00:00:58.302 --> 00:01:02.397
By the end of this module, you should be able to recognize these patterns,

00:01:02.397 --> 00:01:10.547
explain what they are doing, and decide when using them actually makes your code better.

00:01:10.547 --> 00:01:14.342
You do not need to force these techniques into every program.

00:01:14.342 --> 00:01:17.356
The important skill is knowing when they are useful.
